 ### Custom icons and popover content
 
+An optional `hover: { Content }` on the button renders an interactive preview on desktop hover
+or keyboard focus. It receives the same props as popover content, including `close()`, and runs
+under the installation's SDK, query and theme context. Content mounts only while the preview is
+open. Paseo owns anchoring, bounds, padding and vertical scrolling; the pointer can cross from
+the trigger into the preview to scroll or use controls. Compact and native clients keep the
+existing press behavior and do not mount hover content.
+
+Focus the button and press Arrow Down to focus the first preview control. Enter and Space keep
+the button's existing press behavior. Escape dismisses the preview; focus returns to the button
+if it was inside the preview, and otherwise stays where it is. Pressing the button dismisses the
+preview before running its behavior. Pane or workspace navigation, host disconnect, hiding,
+disabling and removal also dismiss it. Label and title updates preserve mounted preview state;
+replacing the hover component closes it. Keep plugin preferences outside the content component
+when they must survive closing and reopening. `title` remains the accessible label and sheet
+title when a custom preview replaces the tooltip.
+
 `PluginButtonIconProps` contains `theme`, `host`, `layout`, `size`, `color`, and the target context.
 Render a React Native icon or indicator within the supplied size. Paseo bounds the icon slot and
 owns all pointer interaction. The icon component can use plugin hooks.
